{# The one and only "re-check DNS now" control (DEC-059).

   Every surface that offers a manual DNS check renders THIS component. The
   health page previously had no button at all while ReverifyDomainController's
   own comment claimed it did — a second copy-pasted form is exactly how that
   drift happened, and a shared component is how it stops.

   The check runs live DNS lookups inside the web request, so it is throttled
   to one run per domain per 3 minutes. When the bucket is empty the button
   renders disabled with the remaining wait rather than inviting a click that
   would only be bounced back with a notice.

   Props:
     - domainId (string)
     - label (string)         Button copy while a re-check is available.
     - buttonClass (string)   daisyUI modifiers appended to `btn`.
     - formTestid (string|null)  Optional test hook on the wrapping form.
#}
{% props domainId, label = 'Re-check now', buttonClass = 'btn-sm btn-primary', formTestid = null %}

{% set recheck = domain_recheck_availability(domainId) %}

<form method="post" action="{{ path('dashboard_domain_reverify', { id: domainId }) }}" class="shrink-0"{% if formTestid is not null %} data-testid="{{ formTestid }}"{% endif %}>
    <button type="submit"
            class="btn {{ buttonClass }}"
            data-testid="recheck-dns-button"
            {% if not recheck.isAvailable %}disabled title="We re-check a domain at most once every 3 minutes so we don't hammer your DNS provider."{% endif %}
    >{% if recheck.isAvailable %}{{ label }}{% else %}Re-check available in {{ recheck.cooldownLabel }}{% endif %}</button>
</form>
